  ("Bracketed items in unattributed quotations can be deleted without a signifi cant change of mean-" 0.09203 0.9082 0.81621 0.83269 0.83269 0.01648 0.00482 0.3278 0.0848 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("ing, as in debe (de) ser el cartero ‘it must be the postman’." 0.09203 0.56052 0.83271 0.84919 0.84919 0.01648 0.00482 0.3557 0.0323 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("‘Colloquial’ refers to language that is acceptable in relaxed educated speech but avoided in" 0.09203 0.90818 0.8614 0.87788 0.87788 0.01648 0.00482 0.2288 0.0998 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("formal situations. ‘Familiar’ describes language that may be heard even from educated speakers" 0.09203 0.9082 0.87789 0.89438 0.89438 0.01648 0.00482 0.3331 0.0568 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("in informal situations but should be used cautiously by non-fl uent foreigners. ‘Popular’ describes" 0.09203 0.90821 0.89439 0.91088 0.91088 0.01648 0.00482 0.3365 0.0168 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("forms that some speakers may reject as ‘uneducated’ and which foreign learners should avoid." 0.09203 0.89534 0.91089 0.92738 0.92738 0.01648 0.00482 0.3302 0.0497 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil))
  (11
  ("x Abbreviations and conventions" 0.09052 0.3491 0.04923 0.06828 0.06828 0.01537 0.00456 0.2802 0.0124 "UFSJES+Palatino-Light" 0.0129 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" t)
  ("‘Dialogue’ shows that the words quoted are spoken by fictional characters whose opinions and" 0.09195 0.90814 0.08317 0.09966 0.09966 0.01648 0.00482 0.2943 0.0885 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("language, which are sometimes comical, sexist or in some other way outrageous, should not be" 0.09195 0.90814 0.09967 0.11616 0.11616 0.01648 0.00482 0.3388 0.0832 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("attributed to their author." 0.09195 0.30831 0.11617 0.13265 0.13265 0.01648 0.00482 0.2969 0.0849 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("We use the term ‘Latin America(n)’ rather than ‘Spanish America(n)’ since it should be obvious" 0.09195 0.90809 0.14486 0.16135 0.16135 0.01648 0.00482 0.3474 0.0267 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("that we are not referring to Brazil or to the French-speaking territories, and because the term" 0.09195 0.9081 0.16136 0.17784 0.17784 0.01648 0.00482 0.2580 0.0334 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("‘Spanish American’ potentially annoys Latin Americans as much as ‘British American’ would no" 0.09195 0.90811 0.17786 0.19434 0.19434 0.01648 0.00482 0.3765 0.0729 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("doubt irritate Americans and Canadians." 0.09195 0.43909 0.19436 0.21084 0.21084 0.01648 0.00482 0.3275 0.0508 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("The spelling of Spanish words reflects the Spanish Academy’s latest recommendations, espe-" 0.09195 0.90798 0.22305 0.23953 0.23953 0.01648 0.00482 0.2856 0.0322 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("cially noticeable in such words as guion for guión, rio for rió, crie for crié, etc. (see 44.2.4). In the case" 0.09195 0.908 0.23955 0.25603 0.25603 0.01648 0.00482 0.3487 0.0457 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("of unresolved disputes, e.g. whether one should write an accent on the pronouns este/éste, ese/ése" 0.09195 0.90806 0.25604 0.27253 0.27253 0.01648 0.00482 0.3152 0.0169 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("and aquel/aquél and on the adverb solo/sólo, we show both forms but recommend the Academy’s" 0.09195 0.90797 0.27254 0.28903 0.28903 0.01648 0.00482 0.3463 0.0326 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("advice, which is to omit the accent." 0.09195 0.38892 0.28904 0.30552 0.30552 0.01648 0.00482 0.3707 0.0605 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("On hearing, out of context, a verb form like habla ‘she/he/you/it speak(s)’, Spanish-speakers do" 0.09195 0.90802 0.31773 0.33422 0.33422 0.01648 0.00482 0.3318 0.0265 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("not automatically form a mental image of a male grammatical subject. For this reason we trans-" 0.09195 0.90807 0.33423 0.35071 0.35071 0.01648 0.00482 0.3883 0.0282 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("late such forms by ‘(s)he speaks’ even though the other possibilities − ‘you speak’ (usted) and ‘it" 0.09195 0.90813 0.35073 0.36721 0.36721 0.01648 0.00482 0.3212 0.0310 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("speaks’ − are not usually shown. If only ‘she’ or ‘he’ appears in the translation of an attributed" 0.09195 0.90818 0.36722 0.38371 0.38371 0.01648 0.00482 0.3037 0.0634 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("example this reflects the gender of the character in the original text. When a third-person plural" 0.09195 0.90812 0.38372 0.40021 0.40021 0.01648 0.00482 0.3494 0.0728 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("verb appears without a pronoun, e.g. reciben ‘they receive’, it must be remembered that the" 0.09195 0.90802 0.40022 0.41671 0.41671 0.01648 0.00482 0.2892 0.0387 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("translation could also be ‘you receive’ (ustedes reciben) if the meaning of the sentence or phrase" 0.09195 0.90798 0.41672 0.4332 0.4332 0.01648 0.00482 0.2819 0.0927 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("allows it." 0.09195 0.16992 0.43322 0.4497 0.4497 0.01648 0.00482 0.4189 0.0561 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
