  ("• Misleading genders of some French nouns (Section 1.4)" 0.10919 0.599 0.27728 0.29376 0.29376 0.01648 0.00482 0.3220 0.0117 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("1.1 Gender of nouns: general" 0.09195 0.48786 0.32205 0.34631 0.34631 0.02425 0.00789 0.2709 0.0394 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 0 "UFSJES+Univers" nil)
  ("Spanish nouns are either masculine or feminine except for a few nouns of undecided gender" 0.09195 0.908 0.35328 0.36976 0.36976 0.01648 0.00482 0.2613 0.0675 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("listed at 1.3.15. The whole question of the gender of Spanish nouns becomes clearer if we divide" 0.09195 0.90812 0.36978 0.38626 0.38626 0.01648 0.00482 0.3294 0.0466 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("them into two groups:" 0.09195 0.28125 0.38628 0.40276 0.40276 0.01648 0.00482 0.3725 0.0437 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("(A) Nouns that refer to human beings and to a few well-known animals: Section 1.2." 0.09195 0.80629 0.41497 0.43145 0.43145 0.01648 0.00482 0.3763 0.0278 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("(B) Nouns that refer to lifeless things, to plants and to the animals not included in group A:" 0.09195 0.90794 0.44366 0.46014 0.46014 0.01648 0.00482 0.2874 0.0246 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
