  ("1.2 Group A: gender of nouns referring to human beings" 0.09195 0.85686 0.50492 0.52918 0.52918 0.02425 0.00789 0.3129 0.0394 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 0 "UFSJES+Univers" nil)
  ("and to a few animals" 0.1456 0.42794 0.52787 0.55213 0.55213 0.02425 0.00789 0.3994 0.0505 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 0 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" t)
  ("As one might expect, nouns that denote males are masculine, and nouns referring to females" 0.09195 0.90816 0.5591 0.57558 0.57558 0.01648 0.00482 0.2945 0.0232 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("are feminine, so el hombre ‘man’, la mujer ‘woman’, el toro ‘bull’, la vaca ‘cow’. This rule applies to" 0.09195 0.90808 0.57559 0.59208 0.59208 0.01648 0.00482 0.3992 0.0261 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("almost all human beings but only to a few animals, many of them listed in 1.2.1. The gender of" 0.09195 0.9081 0.59209 0.60858 0.60858 0.01648 0.00482 0.3636 0.0572 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("other animals is discussed at 1.3.1." 0.09195 0.38378 0.60859 0.62507 0.62507 0.01648 0.00482 0.3372 0.0448 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("The gender of the nouns in group A is more logical in Spanish than in French, where the mas-" 0.09195 0.90793 0.63728 0.65377 0.65377 0.01648 0.00482 0.3045 0.0322 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("culine noun le professeur can refer to a woman. Forms like la recluta ‘recruit’, la centinela ‘sentry’" 0.09195 0.90806 0.65378 0.67026 0.67026 0.01648 0.00482 0.3176 0.0518 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("were applied to men in the past, but we now say el recluta, el centinela for a man and la recluta, la" 0.09195 0.90806 0.67028 0.68676 0.68676 0.01648 0.00482 0.3691 0.0418 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("centinela for a woman." 0.09195 0.27973 0.68678 0.70326 0.70326 0.01648 0.00482 0.3790 0.0699 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("Exceptions: a few nouns of fi xed gender like la víctima or la celebridad may refer to males or to" 0.09195 0.90802 0.71547 0.73195 0.73195 0.01648 0.00482 0.3046 0.1000 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Bold" t)
  ("females: see 1.2.11 for a list." 0.09195 0.32447 0.73196 0.74845 0.74845 0.01648 0.00482 0.3474 0.0701 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("(1) Note that usually the plural masculine form of these nouns is used for mixed sex groups: los" 0.09195 0.90814 0.76066 0.77714 0.77714 0.01648 0.00482 0.3392 0.0225 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Bold" t)
  ("gatos = ‘cats’ as well as ‘tom cats’, mis tíos = ‘my aunt(s) and uncle(s)’ as well as ‘my uncles’, los" 0.09195 0.90821 0.77715 0.79364 0.79364 0.01648 0.00482 0.3673 0.0406 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("padres = ‘parents’ as well as ‘fathers’. See 1.2.8." 0.09195 0.48421 0.79365 0.81014 0.81014 0.01648 0.00482 0.3195 0.0500 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
